== Derivations

- *[d1]* S = cost.s of each verified, non-warm-up record (\`total\_gae \/ √r\`, stored by the runner); mean, median, min, max and sample stdev (stats.rs) are over those records.
- *[d2]* 95% percentile bootstrap interval of the mean S: 4000 resamples of the verified runs of the cell with replacement (stats::bootstrap\_ci, seed 20261002). A cell with one run has no interval. Not a significance test.
- *[d3]* total gae and S \/ floor are means over the verified runs of the cell of cost.total\_gae and boundaries.ratio\_to\_floor; floor S is boundaries.floor\_s = √(π \/ 2A), A = automorphisms the curve offers a generic method.
- *[d4]* expected S is methods::expected\_s(method, A): the closed form the method's mean S approaches as r grows (set-up omitted). A reference mark, not a measurement.
- *[d5]* scaling: per arm, per curve, the mean gae over the arm's verified runs on that curve; the line is ordinary least squares of log2(mean gae) on log2(r) over the curves (bounds::ols), slope α, intercept log2 C so gae = C·r^α. The standard error of α is √(SS\_res\/(sizes−2)\/S\_xx) from those residuals (none below 3 sizes). Counted operations, one point per size: it is not the cluster-bootstrap interval of \`ecbench bound fit\`, which resamples runs and sizes.
- *[d6]* counters (distinguished points, steps) and field operations (muls, sqrs, invs) are means over the cell's verified runs of the counters the record carries (steps = \`steps\`, or baby + giant steps for BSGS); a dash means the method did not count it (unknown, not zero).
- *[d7]* wall and CPU are medians over the cell's verified runs of time.solve\_wall\_ns and time.user\_ns + sys\_ns. The figure is admitted only when every run behind it earned the level the spec requires (compare.rs's gate); otherwise it is informative at the lowest level earned, and never a result.
- *[d8]* phase share = the phase's mean gae over the sum of the arm's mean gae across phases on that curve, over verified runs.
